# ci/kit-calls.rules: the rules `make kit-calls` holds the port's checks
# to (the source-rules check in .chainguard/ci/lint.yaml runs it).
# proved-port-calls reads the configuration `chainctl checks explain
# --output=json .` resolves, not the check files; its doc comment says
# what each rule holds. One rule a line:
#
#   call CHECK TARGET... [with NAME...]
#     CHECK gates a pull request or push, installs theseus-proved-port,
#     sets no variable but VERUS_THREADS, VERUS_BASE and the NAMEs, and
#     runs `make TARGET` for each TARGET in a step read with certainty.
#   forbid PATH
#     no check runs or names PATH, an in-tree copy the kit replaced.
#
# A call check runs on every change: one with a `when: {changed: [...]}`
# list fails its rule, since a list that names none of the paths the
# target reads would let it pass unrun. A check that splits Kani between
# instances (a foreach of KANI_SHARD, KANI_ONLY or KANI_HARNESS, as
# verus.yaml's header describes) cannot be a call check either: the
# tool refuses every KANI_ variable, since it cannot tell that the
# instances cover every harness. List only the unsplit kani and
# kani-main here; a port that splits them deletes their lines and says
# why below.
#
# The lines below are the template's checks. A port adds a call line for
# each check of its own that runs a kit target (verus-amd64, if it
# uncomments it), and deletes the kani lines if it leaves Kani out.
call verus verus-headers verus
call verus-main verus-headers verus
call kani kani
call kani-main kani
call source-rules lint-unsafe kit-calls

# The in-tree copies the kit's targets replaced. A forbid line holds a
# path the port no longer has: a port that keeps a script of its own at
# one of these paths (a rule the kit's target does not cover) drops that
# line, or renames its script. ci/lint-unsafe.sh is not listed: ports
# keep their own SAFETY: comment check there, which `make lint-unsafe`
# does not replace.
forbid verus/count
forbid verus/make
forbid verus/kani/run.sh
forbid ci/kani-regular.sh
forbid ci/heap-noalias.sh
forbid ci/glibc-max.sh
forbid ci/skip-summary.sh
forbid ci/known-failures.sh
